  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 6,000eb<br>\n<strong>Humanity Loss:</strong> 14 (4d6)</p>\n<p>Neuralware. Borgware. Requires 2 Neuralware Option Slots and 2 Internal Option Slots.<br>\nDuration: 5 rounds (15 seconds)<br>\nPrimary Effects:<br>\n+4 to Initiative.<br>\n+2 to Stealth.<br>\nSecondary Effects (Limit 2 per Round):<br>\nBonus to Stealth is increased to +4 until the end of the round (Does not stack with itself).<br>\nIncrease MOVE by 2, to a maximum of 11.<br>\nGain +2 to Evasion against a single target until the end of the round (Does not stack with itself and can be used once per round).</p>\n<p>Note: Activating the Kagekaze causes the user to suffer 1d6 Humanity Loss. The Kagekaze may only be safely activated once per hour. Each time the Sandevistan is activated again before an hour can pass, the humanity loss is doubled, to 2d6, then 4d6, etc. until an hour is allowed to pass. Using any of the Secondary Effects will cause the user to suffer 3 Humanity Loss each time they are used.</p>\n<p><strong>Type:</strong> Neuralware<br>\n<strong>Option Slots:</strong> uses 2</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Activate it like the core Sandevistan: the Primary Effects are toggles in the roll dialog, on by default, and the Secondary Effects are toggles that start off. Turn on only the ones you use.</li>\n<li>It also needs 2 Internal Option Slots.</li>\n<li>The Secondary Effect's MOVE +2 is not automated.</li>\n<li>Humanity Loss for activating it and for each Secondary Effect is not automated.</li>\n<li>The sheet gives no install location, so it uses the core Sandevistan's (Clinic).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From Bontari Homebrew Cyberpunk Items by Bontari (Sandevistans).</em></p>"
  },
